{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>This time my husband will be joined.</b> Because the matriarchs were prophetesses, and they knew that twelve tribes would come forth from Jacob and he would marry four women, she said: from now on he has no opening of the mouth against me, for I have taken my entire portion in the sons (Bereshit Rabbah 72)." "<b>Therefore.</b> Everyone of whom עַל כֵּן is said is multiplied in population — except Levi, whom the Ark consumed." "<b>And he called his name Levi.</b> In all of them it is written וַתִּקְרָא, but this one is written קָרָא. And there are those who say in Bamidbar Rabbah that the Holy One, blessed be He, sent Gabriel and brought him before Him and called him this name, and gave him twenty-four gifts of priesthood — and on account of לִוָּהוּ in gifts He called him Levi."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {2 "Rashi cites מ״א in these — 'those who say' — and the work named is Bamidbar Rabbah, not Bereshit Rabbah."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:11.853679874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}